      "content": "Listen, I hear you, but you're underestimating the potential risks. Stopping the grapefruit might help, but it's not a guarantee. Statins can cause muscle pain, and if you're already experiencing it, it's a sign your body isn't handling the medication well. I understand your reluctance to visit a clinic, but this could be serious. I can't stress enough the importance of getting checked out. You don't want to risk something more severe, like rhabdomyolysis, which can happen with statin use. Trust me, it's better to be safe and get a professional opinion now. Your health is worth it. Let's get you sorted out properly.",
